{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:KnotsParticlesConfinement.UnstableAtomDecayChannel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"KnotsParticlesConfinement.UnstableAtomDecayChannel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Instances.Real.Lemmas","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.IntermediateValue"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.UnstableAtom.decay_channel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.UnstableAtom.decay_channel","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/unstable-atom-decay-channel.lean#L110-L133","doc":"**Decay channel of an unstable atom**\n([`prop:unstable-atom-decay-channel`]).\n\nOff the boundary variety the violated constraint `λ*` is unique, and an atom\nwhose constraint-violation energy changes sign across `[q₁, q₂]` crosses the\nboundary variety inside it.\n\nBoth conjuncts are derived.  This is the declaration the block's `lean.ref`\nnames; until 2026-08-31 the ref resolved to this file and this file did not\ndeclare it. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:unstable-atom-decay-channel","label":"prop:unstable-atom-decay-channel","md":"quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/unstable-atom-decay-channel.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.UnstableAtom.phase_boundary_crossing","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.UnstableAtom.phase_boundary_crossing","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/unstable-atom-decay-channel.lean#L89-L108","doc":"**Phase-boundary crossing** (manuscript sub-claim (iii)).\n\nAn atom stable at `q₁` and unstable at `q₂` crosses a `q*` where the\nconstraint-violation energy of the violated channel vanishes.\n\n**Derived, by the intermediate value theorem.**  The manuscript's\nConnection-to-phase-boundary paragraph *is* an IVT argument — \"necessarily\ncrosses a `q* ∈ [q₁, q₂]` where `E(λ*, q*) = 0`\" — and it is proved here\nrather than carried as an axiom, which is what the previous encoding did.\n\nContinuity of `E` on `[q₁, q₂]` is a hypothesis; neither this file nor the\nmanuscript establishes it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.UnstableAtom.decay_channel_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.UnstableAtom.decay_channel_unique","kind":"theorem","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/knots-particles-confinement/unstable-atom-decay-channel.lean#L66-L87","doc":"**Uniqueness of the decay channel off the boundary variety** (manuscript\nsub-claim (ii)).\n\nGiven the LP-duality selection input — off the boundary variety, every\npartition minimising the constraint-violation energy equals `lamStar` — any\ntwo energy-minimising partitions coincide.\n\nEvery object is a **parameter**: the partition index type, the minimiser\npredicate, the boundary predicate and the selected channel are the caller's,\nso the hypothesis constrains the caller's data rather than data an instance\nchose.  The conclusion is not the hypothesis: it is the two-sided\nconsequence, reached by composing the selection input with itself through\n`lamStar`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}